  "name": "Chimbangueles (San Benito drumming of Sur del Lago)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Chimbangueles are the Afro-Venezuelan drum ensembles of the southern shore of Lake Maracaibo, in Bobures, Gibraltar and neighbouring towns, that play for San Benito, the Black Franciscan saint, in the processions of his feast from late December into January. A set of drums, traditionally seven, each with its own name and role, is carried in procession and struck with sticks, while a lead singer raises the verses answered by drummers and devotees. The membrane-drum card stands in for the chimbángueles.",
